WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.233
In this walkthrough we'll select
settlements in the queue and prepare
them for instruction, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:15.400
Instructing a settlement tells the
bank how to move the money. It starts
in the queue, not in the instruction form.

3
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:25.833
Pick the items to instruct. Settlements are usually
handled in batches for the same counterparty and
value date, so the checkboxes are the normal way in.

4
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:31.700
Opening Instruct Settlement from
here carries the selection across.

5
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:41.100
The identifiers arrive already filled
in. Nothing is copied by hand, which
matters when a batch runs to dozens of items.

6
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:51.833
The settlement instruction is what completes it. It holds
the account and the payment route the money will follow,
and one instruction is applied across the whole selection.

7
00:00:51.833 --> 00:01:02.167
Preparing the instruction is the final step, and
the count of prepared settlements confirms what is
about to be sent before anything leaves the building.

8
00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:10.333
That completes Instructing Settlements. Every
surface shown here can also be opened from the
agent panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
